  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "The two completed experiments (config_006 and config_021) establish that the scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted/concat multimodal multiprofile setup achieves ~0.72-0.725 accuracy, with weighted fusion marginally better. The largest untested dimension is the RNA encoder: scgpt is a fundamentally different learned representation (generative) compared to scvi (variational), and could capture different biological structure. Config_028 changes only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding all other variables (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) constant, making it a clean single-variable ablation. This is the best use of experiment 3 because it reduces uncertainty about whether the RNA encoder is a bottleneck or whether scvi_n200 is already near-optimal, and the result will strongly inform whether to invest remaining budget in scgpt-based or scvi-based configurations."
}

